      "description": "Watch Portland Timbers vs San Diego highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The stage was set for a thrilling MLS encounter as Portland Timbers hosted San Diego in a clash of tactical wits and individual brilliance. On August 20, 2026 , fans packed the stands to witness a battle where every transition and set piece felt like a potential turning point in a high-stakes league match. A Seesaw Battle in the Opening Half The match ignited early with a high tempo, as both sides looked to establish dominance in the midfield. Ariel Lassiter was the first to enter the referee's book with a yellow card in the 17th minute, reflecting the physical nature of the contest. The deadlock was finally broken in the 29th minute when Kristoffer Velde found the back of the net following a sharp assist from Cole Bassett , giving the Portland Timbers a well-deserved lead. However, San Diego refused to go into the break trailing. In the first minute of stoppage time (45+1'), Lewis Morgan delivered a pinpoint pass to Gabriel Pirani , who clinicaly finished to level the score at 1-1. It was a crucial blow just before the whistle, reshaping the narrative for the second period as both teams retreated to the dressing rooms with everything to play for. Timbers Pull Away in the Second Act Whatever was said in the Portland Timbers locker room worked wonders, as they emerged with renewed vigor. In the 51st minute, Jimer Fory set up Ariel Lassiter , who made up for his earlier booking by restoring the home side's advantage. The momentum was firmly with the hosts, and they doubled down in the 68th minute. Kristoffer Velde turned provider this time, assisting David Da Costa for a strike that made it 3-1. A series of substitutions followed, with San Diego introducing Elias Achouri and Amahl Pellegrino in hopes of a late comeback. Despite the tactical shifts and a few late yellow cards for Oscar Verhoeven and Kevin Kelsy , the Timbers remained composed. The final whistle confirmed a decisive victory for the home side, showcasing their clinical efficiency in front of goal."
